{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1065861-istanbul","id":1065861,"title":"Istanbul","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-03-21T11:16:16-07:00","id":1065861,"title":"Istanbul","content":"I'm looking to pull together a Requiem game set in modern Istanbul in about a month. I'm just setting my rough outline right now and wondering what books there are for the city in CofD. This is what I've got off the top of my head:<br /> <br /> - Ruins of Empire (Mummy)<br /> - After the Fall (Demon)<br /> - Slouching Towards Byzantium (Vampire)<br /> - Demon Seeds (Demon)<br /> - Sothis Ascends (Mummy)<br /> <br /> Are there any sources I've missed? Thanks!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":4433,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","user":"Second Chances","date":". 03-21-2017, 02:19 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-21T11:25:58-07:00","id":1065869,"title":"","content":"Istanbul is <i>such </i>a great city for vampire.<br /> <br /> I'm not sure on sources, but I played in a Requiem chronicle set in Renaissance Istanbul, and ran a V20 Dark Ages game set in the Latin Empire, and as a result I'm just incredibly fond of the Queen of Cities.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12981-romulusgloriosus","name":"RomulusGloriosus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12981_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"342"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-21T12:31:18-07:00","id":1065889,"title":"","content":"Theres two other important mentions to this city:<br /> - Fall of the Camarilla has a setting in Constantinople, during Justinian rule.<br /> - Ancient Mysteries: The Crusades setting speaks about Constatinople during that time. Although theres no much information in quantity, there is in quality: in a certain way, it continues the FotC setting, through the Middle Ages, explaining which covenants ruled the city until the Fourth Crusade, when it was sacked by westener crusaders.<br /> <br /> Other minor mentions:<br /> - Invictus also speaks something about it in its history hapter, but part of the text has been retconned by FotC and Ancient Mysteries.<br /> - Ordo Dracul book: Theres some reference to the rulers of the city just after its fall to the Ottomans in the Azercatil entry.<br /> - Bloodlines: The Chosen has an entry for the Agonists, whose main base was in Constantinople.<br /> - Bloodlines: The Legendary: The Gullikan were born in Costantinople.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>LAND OF THE DAMNED: SPAIN (Spanish): </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/3MHWYm\" target=\"_blank\">Land of the Damned: Spain</a>, <a href=\"https://goo.gl/52b0TX\" target=\"_blank\">Kingdoms of Blood: Spain</a>; Cities of the Damned: <a href=\"https://goo.gl/XFMSSe\" target=\"_blank\">Barcelona</a>, <a href=\"https://goo.gl/AXxdgq\" target=\"_blank\">Valencia</a>, <a href=\"https://goo.gl/zkI5a1\" target=\"_blank\">Carthian Constitution</a> (1812), <a href=\"https://goo.gl/5H8M4s\" target=\"_blank\">Three Arrows Pact</a>: <br /> <br /> <b>OTHERS (Spanish): </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/36HngB\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: The Redemption</a>, <a href=\"https://goo.gl/6B9V8l\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Forgotten</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/247-uxas","name":"Uxas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar247_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"394"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-22T03:29:33-07:00","id":1066215,"title":"","content":"Would you share the chronicle documents with us maybe? I am looking for examples of the way crossover is handled in CoD.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/634-marmaduke","name":"marmaduke","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10